    "releaseDate": null,
    "description": "Collects Cisco Secure Endpoint (AMP for Endpoints) events, audit logs, compromises, computers, vulnerabilities and top malware threats from the Secure Endpoint API v1, each selectable with its own schedule. Event types, audit log types and groups are picked from lists read live from the API (all, only selected, all except selected), so types and groups added later need no reconfiguration. Events use sourcetype cisco:se in the Cisco Security Cloud app's format; audit logs use cisco:se:audit with CIM mappings for Authentication and Change. Accounts (API credential, stored encrypted), inputs and collector status are managed in Splunk Web. Independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Cisco.",
    "classification": {
      "intendedAudience": "Security",
      "categories": [
        "Security, Fraud & Compliance"
      ],
